# Settings for github.com/grafana/dashboard-linter.
exclusions:
  target-instance-rule:
    reason: >
      Service-level dashboard for an HPA-managed deployment (pods with churning
      names). Queries deliberately aggregate across instances and are scoped by
      the namespace/job template variables; a per-instance selector would break
      aggregation during scale events and rollouts.
  template-instance-rule:
    reason: >
      Same rationale as target-instance-rule: pods are ephemeral under HPA, so
      an instance variable would pin queries to dead pods. Per-pod breakdowns
      that matter group by the pod label instead.
  target-rate-interval-rule:
    reason: >
      aviso_sse_connection_duration_seconds is only observed when SSE
      connections close, which is sparse. A fixed 30m window keeps the
      histogram quantiles stable; $__rate_interval would mostly return no data.
  target-job-rule:
    reason: >
      The collapsed "Cluster" row queries kube-state-metrics and cAdvisor
      series (kube_horizontalpodautoscaler_*, container_*, kube_pod_*), which
      are labelled by the platform's own job, not the aviso app job. They are
      scoped by namespace plus a pod/hpa name regex instead. All app-metric
      panels still carry the job=~"$job" matcher.
